WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.360
Here's Loose Ends.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.940
It turns notes into
a draft action list,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.570
with the original
words beside each task.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.053
That matters when
a promise starts with if.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.526
Let's use a short example

00:00:12.526 --> 00:00:14.310
with Priya, Leo and Mina.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.020
These notes are made up.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.501
Paste them here,
keeping each action

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.309
and its condition
on the same line.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.690
Choose This Mac to process
the notes locally.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.430
When the model is ready,

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.930
click Find actions.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.672
This is the actual wait

00:00:29.672 --> 00:00:30.861
from the recorded run.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.772
We got three drafts, and one

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.550
suggestion didn't pass the checks.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.850
Priya's draft is due Friday;

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.370
Leo's says tomorrow.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.843
Those dates stay just
as they were written.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.490
Look at Mina's task.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.501
She'll archive the old checklist

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.100
only if the review passes.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.300
That whole condition stays here,

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.181
right beside the original quote.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.120
Let's make Priya's task clearer.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.847
Open Edit, add
to the project team,

00:01:06.847 --> 00:01:07.560
and save.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.922
The app marks that change as yours

00:01:09.922 --> 00:01:11.370
and keeps the original quote.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.876
Now mark Priya's task done

00:01:15.876 --> 00:01:17.600
for the demo, and export.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.110
The Markdown file
keeps the checkmark,

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.100
your edit and the original source.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.269
Save it before closing the tab.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.670
You can also choose Groq.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.622
That's optional: submitting
there sends your notes

00:01:30.622 --> 00:01:33.496
to Groq, and it may
use paid API credit.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.170
You'll still need
to review the results.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:39.826
A longer meeting test using Groq

00:01:39.826 --> 00:01:41.520
missed a conditional commitment.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.326
A matching quote doesn't mean

00:01:43.326 --> 00:01:44.672
the list has everything.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.651
The app is open source

00:01:48.651 --> 00:01:50.280
under the MIT license.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.560
The model licenses are separate.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:53.951
You'll find the code

00:01:53.951 --> 00:01:55.989
and setup instructions on GitHub.
